AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MP_0001446> "This is a rodent-specific behavior. Whisker trimming and barbering are either normal or abnormal depending on the mouse strain. Barbering is particularly common in C57BL/6 and A2G but nearly unseen in other strains. This term should always be used in relation to the control and strain should be specified.")
