AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MP_0009378> "The endoplasmic reticulum membranes form a complex meshwork of tubular channels, which are often expanded into slitlike cavities called cisternae. The ER takes two forms, rough (or granular), with ribosomes adhering to the outer surface, and smooth (with no ribosomes attached).")
