# Class: <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MP_0009530> (abnormal parotid main excretory duct morphology)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "ISBN:0-683-40008-8") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23209333") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "http://ctrgenpath.net/static/atlas/mousehistology/Windows/digestive/parotide.html") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "http://teachmeanatomy.info/head/organs/parotid-gland/") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MP_0009530> "any structural anomaly of the main excretory tubular canal that connects the parotid gland and the buccal mucosa and secretes a serous saliva into the vestibule of the oral cavity; it arises from the anterior surface of the gland, traversing the masseter muscle; the duct then pierces the buccinator muscle, moving medially, and opens out into the oral cavity near the second upper molar; saliva produced by acinar secretory cells in the glandular body flows sequentially through the intercalated ducts, striated ducts, and excretory ducts")
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasBroadSynonym> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MP_0009530> "abnormal parotid duct morphology")
