AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MP_0010112> "In humans and other tailless primates (e.g. great apes), the coccyx is the remnant or a vestigial tail. It consists of 3-5 separate or fused vertebrae (the coccygeal vertebrae) below the sacrum.")
