AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MP_0011184> "The epiblast cells (appearing on day 8 of human embryonic development) make up a columnar epithelium with dense microvilli on the apical surface. During gastrulation, the epiblast cells undergo epithelial-to-mesenchymal transition and delaminate to become the loose mesenchyme of the primitive streak. The epiblast is present in postimplantation mouse embryos between E5.5-E7.5.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MP_0011184> "absent embryonic epiblast")
