# Class: <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MP_0011833> (abnormal cremaster muscle morphology)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> <https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6490-7723>) <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MP_0011833> "any structural anomaly of the thin layer of skeletal muscle that envelops the spermatic cord and testis of most male mammals in a series of loops; it is a continuation of the obliquus internus, arising from the inguinal ligament and inserting into the crest of the pubis and into the sheath of the rectus abdominis; it is innervated by the genital branch of the genitofemoral nerve and functions to draw the testis up toward the superficial inguinal ring in response to cold or to stimulation of the nerve; in females it is represented by only a few muscle loops that envelop the round ligament of the uterus")
AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MP_0011833> <https://orcid.org/0000-0003-3691-0324>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#created_by> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MP_0011833> "csmith")
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#creation_date> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MP_0011833> "2012-11-30T02:55:12Z")
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasExactSynonym> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MP_0011833> "abnormal cremaster morphology")
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasOBONamespace> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MP_0011833> "MPheno.ontology")
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#id> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MP_0011833> "MP:0011833")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MP_0011833> "In rats, it has been shown that cremaster muscles develop from the gubernacular bulb.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MP_0011833> "abnormal cremaster muscle morphology")
SubClassOf(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MP_0011833> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MP_0000759>)

# Class: <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MP_0011834> (abnormal female preputial gland morphology)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> <https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6490-7723>) <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MP_0011834> "any structural anomaly of the paired, lobulated, modified sebaceous glands located on the side of the clitoris in female rodents; in contrast to the preputial glands in male rodents, clitoral glands are a minor source of olfactory stimuli contributing to sexual attractivity; unlike other sebaceous glands, they undergo progressive atrophy of the glandular portion with marked ductal ectasia as rodents age; there is no true anatomical equivalent in humans")
AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MP_0011834> <https://orcid.org/0000-0003-3691-0324>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#created_by> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MP_0011834> "csmith")
