# Class: <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MP_0012103> (abnormal bilaminar embryonic disk morphology)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> <https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6490-7723>) <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MP_0012103> "any structural anomaly of the flattened, almost circular bilaminar plate of cells formed when the inner cell mass (aka embryoblast) forms two epithelial layers, each of a distinct lineage, separated by an extracellular basement membrane: the external (dorsal) layer is called the epiblast and the internal (ventral) layer is called the hypoblast (aka primitive endoderm); together, they compose the bilaminar embryonic disc")
AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MP_0012103> <https://orcid.org/0000-0003-3691-0324>)
