AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#id> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MP_0012126> "MP:0012126")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MP_0012126> "The human placenta is hemomonochorial, as this membrane consists of a single layer of synctiotrophoblast at term. In mice maternal blood bathes a perforated layer of cytotrophoblast cells that overlay two layers of syncytiotrophoblast, thus the murine placenta is hemotrichorial. Maternal blood has direct access to the murine synctiotrophoblast layer I via fenestrations in the murine cytotrophoblast layer.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MP_0012126> "abnormal placenta hemotrichorial membrane morphology")
SubClassOf(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MP_0012126> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MP_0001711>)

