AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#id> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MP_0030367> "MP:0030367")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:15790973") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23300083") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:8911474") rdfs:comment <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MP_0030367> "In mice and rats, the posterior frontal suture (analogous to the human metopic suture) is the only cranial suture that fuses naturally during the first month of life; fusion proceeds in a defined temporal sequence from an anterior to posterior direction, while all other cranial sutures remain patent throughout the life of the animal")
