# Class: <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MP_0030544> (abnormal enamel development)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "GO:0097186") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tooth_enamel") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MP_0030544> "any anomaly in the process whose specific outcome is the formation of dental enamel, the hard outer coating of the exposed portion of the tooth; amelogenesis occurs after the first establishment of dentin, via cells known as ameloblasts, and can generally be divided into two broad stages: (i) a secretory stage that involves proteins and an organic matrix forming a partially mineralized enamel and (ii) a maturation stage which completes enamel mineralization")
AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/creator> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MP_0030544> <https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6490-7723>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/date> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MP_0030544> "2018-01-19T14:29:36Z"^^xsd:dateTime)
