# Class: <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MP_0030844> (abnormal pubis body morphology)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pubis_(bone)") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://medical-dictionary.thefreedictionary.com/body+of+pubis") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MP_0030844> "any structural anomaly of the flattened medial portion of the pubic bone entering into the pubic symphysis; superior and inferior rami extend from it; the body forms one-fifth of the acetabulum, contributing by its external surface both to the lunate surface and the acetabular fossa; its internal surface enters into the formation of the wall of the lesser pelvis and gives origin to a portion of the obturator internus")
AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/creator> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MP_0030844> <https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6490-7723>)
