# Class: <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MP_0031097> (conjunctival chemosis)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "HP:0012375") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://link.springer.com/referenceworkentry/10.1007%2F978-3-642-35951-4_765-1") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MP_0031097> "abnormal swelling (or edema) of the conjunctiva; in chemosis, the integrity of conjunctival capillaries is compromised, leading to increased permeability and leakage of serous fluid; causes include conjunctival irritation, infection, inflammation, trauma, and severe intraorbital inflammation")
