# Class: <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MP_0031246> (abnormal CCL3 level)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://link.springer.com/referenceworkentry/10.1007%2F978-94-007-7696-8_27") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MP_0031246> "deviation from the normal levels of CCL3 protein, a chemokine that is secreted by a variety of hematopoietic and non-hematopoietic cells upon stimulation and plays a key role in recruiting inflammatory cells (macrophages, lymphocytes, eosinophils and basophils) to sites of injury or inflammation via the CCR1 or CCR5 receptor; it helps promote wound healing by recruiting macrophages to sites of tissue injury; acts as a potent osteoclast activator and induces bone resorption; exerts HIV-suppressive activity; and inhibits hematopoietic stem cell proliferation")
