AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:33662810") rdfs:comment <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MP_0031679> "Nuclear shape depends on the cell type. For instance, human fibroblasts harbor a more or less elongated but often smoothly ovoidal nucleus, whereas several immune cells, such as neutrophils, display a highly irregular lobulated nucleus. Nuclear shape abnormalities are common and can be found in healthy cells and in pathological conditions.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MP_0031679> "abnormal cell nucleus shape")
