AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31031767") rdfs:comment <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MP_0031703> "Together with IFN-beta, type I IFNs comprise multiple IFN-alpha subtypes (11 in mice and 13 in humans), IFN-epsilon, IFN-kappa, and IFN-omega in most mammals. In addition, IFN-delta, IFN-zeta (limitin), and IFN-tau have been detected exclusively in pigs, mice, and ruminants, respectively. In addition to being induced in response to viruses, they are also produced in immune responses to other classes of pathogens covering bacteria, parasites, and fungi.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MP_0031703> "abnormal interferon type I secretion")
