# Class: <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MP_0031727> (P wave inversion)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://ecg.utah.edu/pdf/") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://litfl.com/p-wave-ecg-library/") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MP_0031727> "a downward (negative) deflection of the P wave in ECG leads where the wave is typically upright, signaling that the electrical impulse originates outside the sinus node; it indicates retrograde (backward) atrial activation, often originating from the atrioventricular junction or lower atrium")
AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000233> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MP_0031727> <https://github.com/mgijax/mammalian-phenotype-ontology/issues/4269>)
